course: dictionary
lesson: 8940
title: Silent and its meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Silent has more than one meaning, and the words around it tell you which one you need. «The Queen is silent» means she is not speaking, because the sentence is about a conversation. Ask yourself: what word would fit here? Then try your meaning in the sentence and check that it still makes sense.
explain: Silent can also describe a place or a movement that makes no sound at all. «Soft fringed feathers make their flight silent.» An owl's flight makes no noise, so silent means completely quiet.
explain: A silent letter is written in a word but not said. The k in knife is silent: you write it, but you do not say it. Silent reading means reading to yourself without talking.
fact: Silent means making no sound at all; completely quiet.
fact: A silent person is not speaking.
fact: A silent letter is written in a word but not said, like the k in «knee».
fact: Silent letters appear in many English words: k in knife, w in write, b in lamb, h in hour, t in listen.
fact: Context means the words and sentences around a word, and they give clues to its meaning.
exercise: «Soft fringed feathers make their flight silent.» What does silent mean here? | Hungry for food | *Making no sound at all | Very loud and fast | Painted in bright colours
exercise: Which letter is silent in the word knife? | i | *k | f | w
exercise: «When garden birds suddenly fall silent, one of them has often seen a cat.» What does silent mean here? | Singing very loudly | Flying away very fast | *Stopped making any sound | Eating seeds from the feeder
test: What does silent mean in «the Queen is silent»? | Shouting at the top of her voice | Singing a happy song | *Not speaking | Dancing in a circle
test: Which word has a silent b? | *lamb | lamp | lantern | lap
exam: Which sentence uses silent to mean making no sound at all? | *«Soft fringed feathers make their flight silent.» | «The Queen turns crimson and screams.» | «Ava started answering the voice.» | «Alice says Nonsense!»
